<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ordoño II of León</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 924</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ordoño II was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-iii-of-asturias">Alfonso III of Asturias</a> who received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a> when his father's realm was divided in 910. On the death of his brother García I in 914 he also became king of León, made the city of León his royal seat and so gave the kingdom its name. He fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate-of-cordoba">Emirate of Córdoba</a> with mixed success and died in 924.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ordono-ii-of-leon.jpg" alt="Ordoño II of León" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ordono_II_of_Le%C3%B3n_Leon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The realm was divided among his sons: García I took León, the new centre of royal power, <b>Ordoño II</b> took Galicia, and Fruela II took Asturias itself.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-asturias">Kingdom of Asturias · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>When García died in 914 <b>Ordoño II</b> reunited most of the inheritance and made León his royal seat, and historians date the kingdom's name from this transfer of the capital from Oviedo.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-leon">Kingdom of León · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>With <b>Ordoño II of León</b> he took Nájera and La Rioja in the 920s, although Abd al-Rahman III of Córdoba defeated the Christians at Valdejunquera in 920 and sacked Pamplona in 924.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-navarre">Kingdom of Navarre · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In Navarre, the army of Abd al-Rahman III of Córdoba defeated the combined forces of <b>Ordoño II of León</b> and Sancho Garcés I of Pamplona, capturing several leading men.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/july-26">26 July in history</a></li><li><blockquote>When Alfonso III of Asturias was deposed in 910, his son <b>Ordoño II</b> took Galicia as his kingdom.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-galicia">Kingdom of Galicia</a></li></ul></section>
